@sjanoe123 

Issues like this often come down to not having a clear per‑request execution record once retries or provider‑side limits kick in. When a few prompts trigger quota/403 behavior unexpectedly, it’s hard to reconstruct which request crossed what boundary and why.

If helpful context, AI Badgr focuses on generating per‑request receipts (latency, retries/429s, failure stage, token usage/cost) so teams can explain these limit interactions post‑hoc.
